loyed ease so chromosome  arm deletions or duplications  entire chromosomes and any anything uh  shorter than that can be depicted with a  copy number tool  and also with our maps  again as you can see here another  question here can this method detect  mosaics  yes absolutely we talked about the one  percent allele fraction  so we can detect uh mosaic samples  absolutely  surely uh depending on the amount of  coverage that you can get we can go as  low as one percent um and uh  and and so yes we have plenty of  examples of  mosaic cases for fshd for a number of  other  genetic diseases  we don't have a lot of time left we'll  maybe  answer two more questions i am aware of  advantages of these long-range  sequencing platforms but it comes with  major limitations of high error rates  around fifty percent in case of  like iron nanopore how accurate is  optical mapping reads as compared to  center or illumina  what is the error rate you have observed  in general it's a bit of a complicated  question  of course because we're comparing  sequencing methods where you read  the a c g's and t's with a method like  ours that just calls the structural  variance  by looking at these changes in label  patterns  so yes for nanopore sequencing the error  rate this is about the range that you  called for pac bio it's actually a lot  lower i think the main difference  between our technology  and sequencing based methods is that we  are the only technology that can call  these structural variants  genome-wide unbiased with this very high  sensitivity so  it's not a fair comparison because we  don't give you single base pairs  we can't show you these smallest  variants but when it comes to structural  variants there's just no comparison in  our performance  versus the long-range sequencing  platforms and there's actually quite a  few  neutral studies like from the human  genome and sp consortium  that proved that  i think that is all the time we have  any questions that we were not able to  address  during the live periods will be  addressed  by ben clifford or me via the contact  information that you provided when you  registered so with that i'd like to  thank  ben clifford for his time today and all  of you for joining  uh we want to thank lapra roots for  organizing today's  educational webcast as well on the top  left in the resources tab  you have access to our sapphire platform  brochure nrsv white paper  and please contact us at info binance  genomics.com  with any questions that you may have  this webcast can be viewed on demand  uh lab roots will alert you via email  when it's available for replay  and we encourage you that you share this  with your colleagues who may have missed  today's event there's a survey that will  pop up on your screen right now we  appreciate your participation  and with that thank you and until next  time bye
 

